Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/hardware/biometrics/CryptoObject.java at android-15.0.0_r1
(Apache-2.0), batch G: getOpId leaves out the identity credential and the presentation session.

Why: CryptoObject.getOpId asks IdentityCredential and PresentationSession for the credential store's operation handle,
which the public API of those classes does not have (it is a hidden method of the credential store's own binder), and
Minato has no credential store service (android.security.identity is not taken): no identity credential can be made here,
so no handle is ever asked for, and an instanceof of their compile-only stubs would throw NoClassDefFoundError for every
crypto object. The patch drops the two branches.

--- a/core/java/android/hardware/biometrics/CryptoObject.java
+++ b/core/java/android/hardware/biometrics/CryptoObject.java
@@ -163,11 +163,10 @@
             return 0;
         } else if (mCrypto instanceof Long) {
             return (long) mCrypto;
-        } else if (mCrypto instanceof IdentityCredential) {
-            return ((IdentityCredential) mCrypto).getCredstoreOperationHandle();
-        } else if (mCrypto instanceof PresentationSession) {
-            return ((PresentationSession) mCrypto).getCredstoreOperationHandle();
         }
+        // An identity credential or a presentation session has the credential store's operation handle in AOSP. That
+        // store is the system's and Minato has none: no credential is made here, and the compile-only stubs of the
+        // two classes cannot even be asked with instanceof.
         return AndroidKeyStoreProvider.getKeyStoreOperationHandle(mCrypto);
     }
 }
